# Cloudflare Pages headers, copied to the root of dist/ at build time.
#
# Two things this file has already got wrong, both worth remembering:
#
# 1. Rules match the REQUEST PATH, not the file served. A visitor requests
#    "/", which does not match "/index.html". Listing only the latter meant
#    the entry point was served with default caching while /assets/* stayed
#    immutable, so a browser holding stale HTML kept loading the bundle that
#    HTML referenced.
# 2. Indented lines inside a rule are parsed as "Name: value" headers. A
#    comment indented under a rule is a parse error, so every comment here
#    starts at column zero.

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Vite fingerprints every asset filename, so these are safe to cache forever.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Security headers only. Deliberately no Cache-Control here: a broad rule
# would collide with the specific ones above and the precedence between
# overlapping rules is not worth depending on.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Deliberately NOT set: Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy. Enabling it would
# require every basemap tile response to carry Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy,
# which OpenFreeMap does not send, and the map would silently stop loading.
# WebCodecs only needs a secure context, which Pages provides over HTTPS.
